{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017GQGVdTekNkCsKqtFNJ5xM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# SYMBOLS.md — exported-symbol parity (Phase A / Phase D)\n2\t\n3\tThe C project (`c_src/CMakeLists.txt`) builds an **executable** (`add_executable(driver src/main.c)`).\n4\tFor symbol-level differential testing the same single translation unit is also\n5\tbuilt as a shared object, exactly as the task prescribes:\n6\t\n7\t```\n8\tgcc -shared -fPIC -o build_c/libdriver_c.so c_src/src/main.c\n9\t```\n10\t\n11\tThe Rust side is built as a `cdylib` from the same sources that produce the\n12\t`driver` binary (`src/lib.rs` + `src/driver_impl.rs`):\n13\t\n14\t```\n15\tcargo build            # -> target/debug/libdriver.so  (+ target/debug/driver)\n16\trustc --edition 2021 --crate-type cdylib -o libdriver_rs.so src/lib.rs   # what the tests build\n17\t```\n18\t\n19\t## `nm -D --defined-only` — C shared object\n20\t\n21\t| symbol | type | C declaration | exported by Rust `.so`? |\n22\t|--------|------|---------------|-------------------------|\n23\t| `driver` | `T` (global text) | `void driver(int x)` | YES — `#[no_mangle] pub extern \"C\" fn driver(x: c_int)` in `src/lib.rs` |\n24\t| `main`   | `T` (global text) | `int main(void)` | YES — `#[no_mangle] pub extern \"C\" fn main() -> c_int` in `src/lib.rs` |\n25\t\n26\tThat is the complete list; the C `.so` defines exactly two global symbols.\n27\t\n28\t### Deliberately **not** exported\n29\t\n30\t| C entity | why not exported |\n31\t|----------|------------------|\n32\t| `static void print_hex(unsigned char *p, int len)` | `static` ⇒ internal linkage, absent from `nm -D` of the C `.so`. Translated as the private `imp::print_hex` and reached through `driver`. |\n33\t\n34\t## Undefined symbols\n35\t\n36\t`nm -D --undefined-only` on the C `.so`:\n37\t`__isoc99_scanf`, `printf`, `putchar` (glibc) plus the usual weak\n38\t`_ITM_*` / `__gmon_start__` / `__cxa_finalize` toolchain stubs.\n39\t\n40\tOn the Rust `.so`: glibc (`read`, `write`, `writev`, `malloc`, `memcpy`, …),\n41\tthe `pthread_*`/`__tls_get_addr` TLS helpers and the `_Unwind_*` family from\n42\t`libgcc_s.so.1`. All are satisfied by `DT_NEEDED` entries\n43\t(`libgcc_s.so.1`, `libc.so.6`, `ld-linux-x86-64.so.2`), i.e. **zero\n44\tmissing/undefined non-libc(-runtime) symbols**.\n45\t\n46\t## Result\n47\t\n48\t```\n49\t$ nm -D --defined-only build_c/libdriver_c.so | awk '{print $3}' | sort   >  c.txt\n50\t$ nm -D --defined-only libdriver_rs.so        | awk '{print $3}' | sort   >  rs.txt\n51\t$ diff c.txt rs.txt      # empty\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\tSymbol diff is **empty** — every symbol exported by the C `.so` is exported by\n55\tthe Rust `.so` under the exact same name, and the Rust `.so` exports nothing\n56\textra. Enforced automatically by `tests/symbols.rs`\n57\t(`c_and_rust_export_identical_symbol_sets`), which re-runs `nm -D` on both\n58\tobjects and also checks the cargo-built `target/{debug,release}/libdriver.so`\n59\twhen present.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WWzRbn7bLfFQz47QHjaCxx","session_id":"64daaee6-dfd8-4ebc-87be-dd6361eb86bc","uuid":"de6f2473-8b8b-4043-ab15-a472c8314366","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:48:08.815Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Audit verification artifacts"}
