{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BKg37jes1mBWmtXqJEsUAw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CONFIGS.md — configuration-surface table (Phase A → Phase B)\n2\t\n3\t## Mechanical derivation of the axes\n4\t\n5\tEverything below is derived from `c_src/src/main.c` and `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`.\n6\t\n7\t* **Build-time configuration.** `CMakeLists.txt` is\n8\t  `cmake_minimum_required(3.10)` + `project(driver)` + `add_executable(driver\n9\t  src/main.c)` — no `option()`, no `target_compile_definitions`, no\n10\t  `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` branches. The C source contains **zero** `#ifdef`/`#if`\n11\t  (`grep -c '#if\\|#ifdef\\|#ifndef' c_src/src/main.c` → 0). `Cargo.toml` has\n12\t  **no `[features]` section**, so the only feature combination is the empty one\n13\t  (verified with `cargo check --no-default-features` and plain `cargo check`).\n14\t  The two remaining build configurations that *can* change behaviour on the\n15\t  Rust side are the cargo profiles, because `[profile.release]` sets\n16\t  `panic = \"abort\"` and enables optimisation; both are covered\n17\t  (`opt-level=0`/`debug-assertions=on` and `opt-level=3`/`panic=abort`).\n18\t* **Runtime options/flags.** None. `main` takes no `argc`/`argv`, reads no\n19\t  environment variable, has no locale call, no getopt, no config file. The only\n20\t  runtime inputs are (a) the `int` argument of `driver` and (b) the byte stream\n21\t  on stdin consumed by `scanf(\"%d\", &x)`.\n22\t* **Public entry points** (`nm -D` on the C `.so`, see `SYMBOLS.md`):\n23\t  `driver` (the low-level entry point — call it directly, do not only drive it\n24\t  through `main`) and `main` (the one-shot wrapper: `scanf` + `driver`).\n25\t  `print_hex` is `static`, exercised through `driver`.\n26\t* **Input shapes the code actually distinguishes.**\n27\t  * `driver`/`print_hex`: the 4 bytes of the `int` in host order; `%02x`\n28\t    formatting distinguishes bytes `< 0x10` (zero-padded nibble) from\n29\t    `>= 0x10`, and `0x00`/`0xff` are the loop's extremes. Byte order matters\n30\t    (`&x` reinterpreted as `unsigned char*`).\n31\t  * `main`: presence/kind/length of leading whitespace, sign (`none`/`+`/`-`),\n32\t    digit count (1 … thousands), leading zeros, value magnitude relative to the\n33\t    `int`/`unsigned int`/`long` boundaries, trailing junk, trailing newline or\n34\t    not, stdin being a regular file vs a pipe, and input longer than the stdio\n35\t    buffer (4 KiB in glibc, 8 KiB in Rust's `BufReader`).\n36\t* **Call-sequence state.** `driver` is stateless apart from the stdout buffer,\n37\t  but `main` is not: `scanf` leaves the byte it stopped on in the `stdin` FILE\n38\t  (`ungetc`) and sets a sticky EOF indicator, so *calling the exported `main`\n39\t  more than once* is a distinct configuration (row C28). This axis only shows up\n40\t  when the low-level exports are driven directly, which is why the translation\n41\t  keeps that state in `STDIN_PUSHBACK`/`STDIN_EOF` instead of in a local reader.\n42\t* **Process environment.** The C code never calls `setlocale`, so `LC_*`/`LANG`\n43\t  must not change anything (row C29); the `SIGPIPE` disposition inherited from\n44\t  the process start-up is part of this axis too (see ERRORS.md E13).\n45\t\n46\tThe rows below are the pruned cross-product of those axes: every combination\n47\tthe C code treats differently. Each row is exercised with many randomised\n48\tinputs (SplitMix64, fixed seed, see `tests/common/mod.rs`) and compared\n49\tbyte-for-byte between the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` loaded through\n50\t`libloading` (plus, for `main`, the two real executables).\n51\t\n52\t## Table\n53\t\n54\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | test | [x] |\n55\t|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|------|-----|\n56\t| C1 | `driver` (`.so`) | `x == 0` — all four bytes zero, zero-padded nibbles | `c1_driver_zero` | [x] |\n57\t| C2 | `driver` (`.so`) | small magnitudes: every `x` in `-1024..=1024` (single-byte and carry-into-second-byte shapes, positive **and** negative) | `c2_driver_small_magnitudes` | [x] |\n58\t| C3 | `driver` (`.so`) | nibble-padding shapes: every `x` whose bytes are drawn from `{0x00,0x01,0x0f,0x10,0x7f,0x80,0xf0,0xff}` (8⁴ = 4096 combinations, exhaustive) | `c3_driver_nibble_padding_matrix` | [x] |\n59\t| C4 | `driver` (`.so`) | signed boundaries: `INT_MIN`, `INT_MIN+1`, `-1`, `0`, `1`, `INT_MAX-1`, `INT_MAX`, `0x80000000`, `0xffffffff`, all powers of two ±1 | `c4_driver_boundary_values` | [x] |\n60\t| C5 | `driver` (`.so`) | full 32-bit range, randomised: 20 000 uniformly random `i32` (fixed seed) | `c5_driver_random_full_range` | [x] |\n61\t| C6 | `driver` (`.so`) | byte-position sweep: each of the 4 bytes takes every value `0x00..=0xff` while the others hold a fixed non-zero pattern (1024 values) — catches byte-order and per-byte formatting bugs | `c6_driver_byte_position_sweep` | [x] |\n62\t| C7 | `driver` (`.so`) | exhaustive low 16 bits: `x` covers all 65 536 values of `(fixed_high << 16) | low` | `c7_driver_exhaustive_low_16_bits` | [x] |\n63\t| C8 | `driver` (`.so`) | many calls in one process (10 000 consecutive calls, one capture) — accumulated stdio buffering, no separators | `c8_driver_repeated_calls_one_process` | [x] |\n64\t| C9 | `driver` (`.so`) | stdout is a **pipe** instead of a regular file (line- vs fully-buffered stdio path), randomised values | `c9_driver_stdout_is_a_pipe` | [x] |\n65\t| C10 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | no sign, plain decimal digits, randomised `0..=INT_MAX` (400 values) | `c10_main_unsigned_decimal_random` | [x] |\n66\t| C11 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | `-` sign, randomised magnitudes `0..=2^31` (400 values, includes `-0` and `INT_MIN`) | `c11_main_negative_random` | [x] |\n67\t| C12 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | `+` sign, randomised magnitudes (400 values) | `c12_main_explicit_plus_random` | [x] |\n68\t| C13 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | randomised leading-whitespace prefix built from `{' ','\\t','\\n','\\v','\\f','\\r'}` (1–20 bytes) before a randomised number | `c13_main_leading_whitespace_kinds` | [x] |\n69\t| C14 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | randomised number of leading zeros (1–40) before a randomised value, with and without sign | `c14_main_leading_zeros` | [x] |\n70\t| C15 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | valid number followed by trailing junk: letters, punctuation, a second number, more whitespace, `\\0`, high-bit bytes (only the first conversion is performed) | `c15_main_trailing_junk` | [x] |\n71\t| C16 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | line-ending shapes: no trailing newline, `\"\\n\"`, `\"\\r\\n\"`, `\"\\n\\n\"`, digits split by a newline (`\"12\\n34\"` ⇒ only `12`) | `c16_main_line_ending_shapes` | [x] |\n72\t| C17 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | digit-string lengths 1…25 with randomised digits, both signs — walks the whole `int`→`long`→overflow ladder | `c17_main_digit_length_ladder` | [x] |\n73\t| C18 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | huge digit strings: 100 / 1 000 / 4 095 / 4 096 / 4 097 / 8 191 / 8 192 / 8 193 / 20 000 digits (crosses glibc's 4 KiB stdio buffer and Rust's 8 KiB `BufReader`), both signs | `c18_main_huge_digit_strings` | [x] |\n74\t| C19 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | exact numeric boundaries: `INT_MAX±1`, `INT_MIN±1`, `2^31`, `2^32±1`, `UINT_MAX`, `LONG_MAX±1`, `LONG_MIN±1`, `2^63`, `2^64±1`, 10^19, 10^20, plus randomised 64-bit and 128-bit magnitudes with both signs | `c19_main_numeric_boundaries` | [x] |\n75\t| C20 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | stdin is a **pipe** rather than a regular file (unseekable stream, short reads), randomised inputs | `c20_main_stdin_is_a_pipe` | [x] |\n76\t| C21 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | whitespace run longer than both stdio buffers (4 095 / 4 096 / 4 097 / 8 191 / 8 192 / 8 193 / 40 000 blanks) before the number | `c21_main_whitespace_across_buffer_boundary` | [x] |\n77\t| C22 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | embedded `\\0` and non-ASCII/UTF-8 bytes before (matching failure) and after (ignored) the digits | `c22_main_nul_and_non_ascii_bytes` | [x] |\n78\t| C23 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | return value of the exported `main` compared (must be `0`), for a valid and an invalid input | `c23_main_return_value` | [x] |\n79\t| C24 | `driver` + `main` (`.so`) | both entry points driven in the same process, interleaved (`driver`, then `main`, then `driver`) — shared stdout buffer state, and `driver`'s output must not disturb the conversion | `c24_main_and_driver_interleaved`, `c24_driver_state_is_not_sticky` | [x] |\n80\t| C25 | `driver` executable (process level) | the real programs (`c_src/build/driver` vs `cargo`-built `driver`): stdin from a regular file, all input classes of C10–C22, comparing stdout **and** exit status | `c25_executables_stdin_file` | [x] |\n81\t| C26 | `driver` executable (process level) | same, with stdin from a **pipe** and stdout to a pipe | `c26_executables_stdin_pipe` | [x] |\n82\t| C28 | `main` (`.so`, forked) | the exported `main` called **repeatedly in one process** — the composed-pipeline case: glibc's `scanf` keeps the `ungetc` pushback byte and the sticky EOF indicator in the `stdin` FILE, so call *n+1* continues exactly where call *n* stopped. Sub-shapes: several numbers separated by every whitespace kind; a conversion that stops on a non-whitespace byte (`\"12x34\"`, `\"12-34\"` — the pushed-back byte is re-read); reading past EOF; unseekable pipe stdin; unreadable stdin; 20-call drains of long randomised token streams; randomised streams of 1–6 tokens with random separators | `c28_repeated_main_multiple_numbers`, `c28_repeated_main_pushback_byte`, `c28_repeated_main_past_eof`, `c28_repeated_main_pipe_stdin`, `c28_repeated_main_long_stream`, `c28_repeated_main_unreadable_stdin`, `c28_repeated_main_randomised_streams` | [x] |\n83\t| C29 | `driver` executable (process level) | environment/locale axis: `LC_ALL`, `LC_NUMERIC`, `LANG` set to `C`, `POSIX`, `en_US.UTF-8`, `tr_TR.UTF-8`, `de_DE.UTF-8`, `fr_FR.UTF-8` — the C code never calls `setlocale`, so nothing may change | `c29_executables_ignore_the_locale_environment` | [x] |\n84\t| C27 | build configuration | every row above re-run against a Rust `.so` built with `opt-level=0`/`debug-assertions=on` **and** one built with `opt-level=3`/`panic=abort`/`debug-assertions=off` (mirrors `[profile.release]`), and `cargo test` re-run with `--no-default-features` and with default features (the only two feature combinations that exist) | `RUST_SO_PROFILE` env switch + `scripts/verify_all.sh` | [x] |\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WWzRbn7bLfFQz47QHjaCxx","session_id":"64daaee6-dfd8-4ebc-87be-dd6361eb86bc","uuid":"ed1c1398-ac9b-40f6-8a70-10e222908f25","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:48:12.672Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Audit verification artifacts"}
