W|01000000\\n02000000\\n\n$ ./mix librs.so | cat -v   ->  01000000\\n|RAW|02000000\\n\n/* mix2.c: drv(1); printf(\"|PRINTF|\"); drv(2); fflush(NULL); */\n$ ./mix2 libc.so  | cat -v  ->  01000000\\n|PRINTF|02000000\\n\n$ ./mix2 librs.so | cat -v  ->  01000000\\n02000000\\n|PRINTF|\n```\n`CONFIGS.md:63` (C8) claims to cover \"accumulated stdio buffering\" and `CONFIGS.md:79` (C24) \"shared stdout buffer state\", but every child in `tests/common/mod.rs` writes nothing else to fd 1, so the axis is unreachable by the suite. (Under a *tty* stdout the two agree, because glibc then line-buffers — see finding 3.)\n\n---\n\n**3. [WRONG-CLAIM] `CONFIGS.md:64` (C9) — \"stdout is a **pipe** instead of a regular file (line- vs fully-buffered stdio path)\".**\n\nglibc selects line buffering only when `isatty(fd)`; a pipe and a regular file are *both* fully buffered, so C9 does not exercise a different buffering mode at all. Evidence: with stdout a pipe, C is fully buffered (`|RAW|01000000\\n02000000\\n`, finding 2); under a pty it is line-buffered:\n```\n$ script -qc \"./mix libc.so\" /dev/null | cat -v  ->  01000000^M |RAW|02000000^M\n```\nConsequence: the genuine buffering-mode axis (stdout on a terminal) has no CONFIGS.md row and no test.\n\n---\n\n**4. [MISSING-COVERAGE] — concurrency: `driver` records are atomic in Rust but tear in C. No row, no test.**\n\nC emits four `printf(\"%02x\")` + one `putchar`, each taking/releasing the FILE lock; Rust holds `stdout().lock()` for the whole call.\n```c\n/* thr.c: 2 threads x 2000 calls, driver(0x11111111) / driver(0x22222222) */\nlibc.so : lines=4000  torn/mixed lines=1266   e.g. \"11111122222222\", \"2222221122\"\nlibrs.so: lines=4000  torn/mixed lines=0\n```\n`CONFIGS.md` has no thread/reentrancy axis anywhere.\n\n---\n\n**5. [WRONG-CLAIM] `CONFIGS.md:47` — \"Each row is exercised with many randomised inputs (SplitMix64, fixed seed…)\".**\n\nNot true for a large minority of rows; these test bodies contain no `Rng` at all and use fixed/exhaustive value sets: `c1_driver_zero` (`tests/driver_valid.rs:13`, a single hand-picked value `0`), `c3` (:28), `c4` (:46), `c6` (:90), `c7` (:105), `c24_driver_state_is_not_sticky` (:150), `c16` (`tests/main_valid.rs:134`), `c23` (:325), `c24_main_and_driver_interleaved` (:340), `c29` (`tests/executables.rs:98`), and four C28 sub-tests — `c28_repeated_main_multiple_numbers` (`tests/repeat_main.rs:53`), `..._pushback_byte` (:78), `..._past_eof` (:104), `..._pipe_stdin` (:115). (The exhaustive/boundary coverage is fine; the blanket sentence is the inaccuracy.)\n\n---\n\n**6. [WRONG-CLAIM] `CONFIGS.md:84` (C27) — \"`--no-default-features` and with default features (the only two feature combinations that exist)\".**\n\n`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table (`grep -n features Cargo.toml` → no match), so there is exactly **one** combination, the empty one; `--no-default-features` and the default build are byte-identical configurations. This contradicts `CONFIGS.md:12-13`, which states it correctly.\n\n---\n\n**7. [VACUOUS-TEST] `tests/symbols.rs:159` `cargo_built_shared_objects_match_too` passes with zero assertions when the cargo cdylibs are absent, and plain `cargo test` does not build them.**\n\nThe loop `continue`s when `target/{debug,release}/libdriver.so` is missing and only `eprintln!(\"checked {checked} …\")` — no assertion fires. Verified that `cargo test` alone never produces the cdylib (`src/main.rs` re-includes `driver_impl.rs` via `#[path]` rather than depending on the lib, and `[lib] test = false`):\n```\n$ CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/t2 cargo test --offline --no-run   # exit 0\n$ ls $TMPDIR/t2/debug/ | grep driver   ->  driver     (no libdriver.so)\n```\nSo on a clean checkout this test is vacuous. It is non-vacuous only after `cargo build`, which `scripts/verify_all.sh:108-109` does run. `SYMBOLS.md:58-59`'s \"when present\" wording is honest, so the doc is not wrong — the test is conditionally vacuous.\n\n---\n\n**8. [OK-NOTE] E14/E15 are checked `[x]` with \"unreachable\" instead of a test name — the justification is factually correct, but the backing test asserts almost nothing.**\n\n`ERRORS.md:50-51`. The real test is `e14_e15_print_hex_is_not_reachable_through_ffi` (`tests/error_paths.rs:389`); it checks `nm -D` output has no `print_hex` and then only `assert_eq!(c.out.len(), 9)` / `assert_eq!(r.out.len(), 9)` — it never compares C and Rust bytes. I independently confirmed unreachability: `dlsym(h,\"print_hex\")` returns `(nil)` for both `.so`s.\n\n---\n\n**9. [OK-NOTE] E11/E12/E13 compare only exit status, never output bytes — structurally, not by oversight.**\n\n`tests/common/mod.rs:526-530` returns `Vec::new()` for `Stdout::Closed`/`DevFull`/`ClosedPipe`, so `e11` (`tests/error_paths.rs:287`), `e12` (:313) and `e13` (:339) can only detect status divergence. Fine for those rows, but an output-content divergence under those wirings would be invisible.\n\n---\n\n**10. [OK-NOTE] `SYMBOLS.md:16` under-documents the tests' rustc invocation.**\n\nDocumented: `rustc --edition 2021 --crate-type cdylib -o libdriver_rs.so src/lib.rs   # what the tests build`. Actual (`tests/common/mod.rs:148-171`): adds `--crate-name driver -A warnings -C opt-level={0|3} -C debug-assertions={on|off} -C overflow-checks={on|off}` and `-C panic=abort` for `RUST_SO_PROFILE=release`.\n\n---\n\n**11. [OK-NOTE] `scripts/verify_all.sh` feature enumeration is correct; two documented blind spots.**\n\nTested the awk + bitmask powerset against a fake `Cargo.toml` in `$TMPDIR` with `default=[\"alpha\"]`, `alpha`, `beta`, `gamma_1`, `delta-x`: awk emitted exactly the 4 non-`default` names and the loop produced 16 combinations including the empty one (correct powerset, `default` correctly excluded, `[dependencies]` keys correctly not picked up). It would miss implicit features created by `optional = true` dependencies, and requires unquoted keys starting at column 0. Neither applies to this `Cargo.toml`.\n\n---\n\n**12. [OK-NOTE] Everything else in the checklist verified accurate.**\n\n- **SYMBOLS.md**: fresh builds give `T driver`, `T main` on both; `diff c.txt rs.txt` is empty. C undefined set is exactly `__isoc99_scanf`, `printf`, `putchar` + weak `_ITM_*`/`__gmon_start__`/`__cxa_finalize`, as documented. Rust undefined set is glibc + `pthread_*`/`__tls_get_addr` + `_Unwind_*`, all covered by `DT_NEEDED = libgcc_s.so.1, libc.so.6, ld-linux-x86-64.so.2` (`objdump -p`) — matches `SYMBOLS.md:36-44`. `build_c/libdriver_c.so`, `target/debug/libdriver.so`, `target/release/libdriver.so` all export exactly `{driver, main}`.\n- **ERRORS.md**: both greps at `ERRORS.md:9-15` reproduce byte-exactly (grep 1 exit 1/no matches; grep 2 → `24:#include <stdio.h>`, `27:… i < len …`, `41:    return 0;`). I verified **15 of 17** rows empirically against a freshly built C program (E1, E2, E3 both variants, E4 incl. `\\0`/`\\x80`/`\\xff`, E5, E6, E7 incl. 5000 nines → `ffffffff`, E8 → `00000000`, E9 all six documented values → `00000080`/`ffffff7f`/`ffffffff`/`00000000`/`ffffffff`/`00000000`, E10 all 9-byte outputs, E11 fd1 closed → rc 0, E12 `/dev/full` → rc 0, E13 reader-less pipe → `signaled 13`, E17 rc 0 for all inputs). Every \"expected C result\" column is correct. All 15 named test functions exist.\n- **CONFIGS.md**: all 34 named test functions for C1–C26/C28/C29 exist and their bodies match the row descriptions (spot-checked every row: value sets, counts, seeds, `Stdin::Pipe` vs `Stdin::File`, exhaustiveness claims all check out). `CMakeLists.txt` is exactly `cmake_minimum_required(3.10)` + `project(driver)` + `add_executable(driver src/main.c)`, no `option()`; `grep -c '#if\\|#ifdef\\|#ifndef' c_src/src/main.c` → 0. The \"4 KiB glibc / 8 KiB Rust `BufReader`\" claim at `CONFIGS.md:35` is measured-correct (4096 vs 8192 bytes consumed from a pipe). The 6 locale sets in C29 are all installed (`locale -a` → 869 entries), so that row is meaningful.\n- **Differential integrity (item 5)**: every comparison goes through `dlopen`/`dlsym` on the two `.so`s (`tests/common/mod.rs:196-243`); I confirmed the resolved pointers are genuinely distinct and neither aliases the harness's own `main` (`driver: 0x7fbba9bb7193 vs 0x7fbba9b702d0 same=0`; `main: 0x7fbba9bb71b2 vs 0x7fbba9b702e0 same=0`; harness `main=0x401156`). No test compares a value to itself; the hard-coded expectations (`smoke.rs:13-14`, `driver_valid.rs:168`, `main_valid.rs:360`, `executables.rs:149`) are *additional* anchors on top of a real C-vs-Rust comparison, not substitutes for it.\n- **Cargo.toml**: no `[features]` section; `libloading = \"0.8\"` is in `[dev-dependencies]` (`Cargo.toml:22-23`); `[profile.release] panic = \"abort\"` (:25-26).\n- **Test suite passes now** (`timeout 600 cargo test --offline`, exit 0, 64 tests, 0 failures): `unittests src/main.rs` 0 passed; `driver_valid` 10; `error_paths` 20; `executables` 4; `main_valid` 15; `repeat_main` 7; `smoke` 4; `symbols` 4.\n\nI did not execute `scripts/verify_all.sh`: it writes into `c_src/build/` and `build_c/` inside the working directory, which the read-only rule forbids. Nothing in the working directory was modified; all scratch artifacts are under `$TMPDIR`."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":569306,"totalTokens":129438,"totalToolUseCount":37,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1401,"cache_read_input_tokens":119865,"output_tokens":8170,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2887},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1401},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":17,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":20,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
