structions call for regardless of the source:\n61\t`generic_zero_length_and_oversized_input` (empty stdin, 1 MiB of digits, 1 MiB of\n62\twhitespace, 1 MiB of junk) and `e16b_main_called_with_extra_arguments`\n63\t(out-of-signature arguments across the FFI boundary), while\n64\t`tests/executables.rs::known_good_outputs` pins absolute expected bytes so a\n65\tregression that hits *both* implementations cannot pass silently.\n66\t\n67\tTwo notes on what those tests can observe:\n68\t\n69\t* **E14/E15 are documented-unreachable.** `print_hex` is `static`, so the symbol\n70\t  does not exist at the FFI boundary and there is nothing to compare;\n71\t  `e14_e15_print_hex_is_not_reachable_through_ffi` pins exactly that (both `.so`s\n72\t  lack the symbol, and the only reachable length is `sizeof(int)`), so the rows\n73\t  turn into real differential tests the moment someone exports it. The code path\n74\t  itself is covered through `driver` by every C1–C9 row.\n75\t* **E11/E12/E13 can only compare the exit status**, because their whole point is\n76\t  a stdout that cannot receive data (closed fd, `ENOSPC`, no reader). The output\n77\t  content for those wirings is empty by construction on both sides; the content\n78\t  comparisons live in the rows with a working stdout.\n79\t\n80\t### Not emulated (deliberate, documented in CONFIGS.md)\n81\t\n82\t`vfscanf` copies the digit run into a heap scratch buffer, so under an artificial\n83\t`RLIMIT_AS` a multi-megabyte digit run makes the *conversion* fail in C\n84\t(`00000000`) while the translation, which parses in constant memory, still\n85\tsaturates (`ffffffff`). See the \"Deliberately not emulated\" table in\n86\t`CONFIGS.md`; without an artificial memory limit the two agree for every length\n87\ttested (up to 1 MiB of digits).\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014BZJRV9mTTLmVbbGcubu9U","session_id":"64daaee6-dfd8-4ebc-87be-dd6361eb86bc","uuid":"6fb5fe6b-35e3-4746-8186-fd79195656b1","timestamp":"2026-08-18T10:36:55.3