{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01X13uwfYNSg1ZrHDV5K1gya","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# SYMBOLS.md — exported-symbol parity (Phase A / Phase D)\n2\t\n3\tThe C project (`c_src/CMakeLists.txt`) builds an **executable** (`add_executable(driver src/main.c)`).\n4\tFor symbol-level differential testing the same single translation unit is also\n5\tbuilt as a shared object, exactly as the task prescribes:\n6\t\n7\t```\n8\tgcc -shared -fPIC -o build_c/libdriver_c.so c_src/src/main.c\n9\t```\n10\t\n11\tThe Rust side is built as a `cdylib` from the same sources that produce the\n12\t`driver` binary (`src/lib.rs` + `src/driver_impl.rs`):\n13\t\n14\t```\n15\tcargo build                     # -> target/debug/libdriver.so  (+ target/debug/driver)\n16\tcargo build --release           # -> target/release/libdriver.so (panic = \"abort\")\n17\t\n18\t# exactly what tests/common/mod.rs builds and dlopens (RUST_SO_PROFILE=dev|release):\n19\trustc --edition 2021 --crate-type cdylib --crate-name driver -A warnings \\\n20\t      -C opt-level=0 -C debug-assertions=on  -C overflow-checks=on  \\\n21\t      -o libdriver_rs_dev.so     src/lib.rs\n22\trustc --edition 2021 --crate-type cdylib --crate-name driver -A warnings \\\n23\t      -C opt-level=3 -C debug-assertions=off -C overflow-checks=off -C panic=abort \\\n24\t      -o libdriver_rs_release.so src/lib.rs\n25\t```\n26\t\n27\t## `nm -D --defined-only` — C shared object\n28\t\n29\t| symbol | type | C declaration | exported by Rust `.so`? |\n30\t|--------|------|---------------|-------------------------|\n31\t| `driver` | `T` (global text) | `void driver(int x)` | YES — `#[no_mangle] pub extern \"C\" fn driver(x: c_int)` in `src/lib.rs` |\n32\t| `main`   | `T` (global text) | `int main(void)` | YES — `#[no_mangle] pub extern \"C\" fn main() -> c_int` in `src/lib.rs` |\n33\t\n34\tThat is the complete list; the C `.so` defines exactly two global symbols.\n35\t\n36\t### Deliberately **not** exported\n37\t\n38\t| C entity | why not exported |\n39\t|----------|------------------|\n40\t| `static void print_hex(unsigned char *p, int len)` | `static` ⇒ internal linkage, absent from `nm -D` of the C `.so`. Translated as the private `imp::print_hex` and reached through `driver`. |\n41\t\n42\t## Undefined symbols\n43\t\n44\t`nm -D --undefined-only` on the C `.so`:\n45\t`__isoc99_scanf`, `printf`, `putchar` (glibc) plus the usual weak\n46\t`_ITM_*` / `__gmon_start__` / `__cxa_finalize` toolchain stubs.\n47\t\n48\tOn the Rust `.so`: glibc (`read`, `write`, `writev`, `malloc`, `memcpy`, …),\n49\tthe `pthread_*`/`__tls_get_addr` TLS helpers and the `_Unwind_*` family from\n50\t`libgcc_s.so.1`. All are satisfied by `DT_NEEDED` entries\n51\t(`libgcc_s.so.1`, `libc.so.6`, `ld-linux-x86-64.so.2`), i.e. **zero\n52\tmissing/undefined non-libc(-runtime) symbols**.\n53\t\n54\t## Result\n55\t\n56\t```\n57\t$ nm -D --defined-only build_c/libdriver_c.so | awk '{print $3}' | sort   >  c.txt\n58\t$ nm -D --defined-only libdriver_rs.so        | awk '{print $3}' | sort   >  rs.txt\n59\t$ diff c.txt rs.txt      # empty\n60\t```\n61\t\n62\t### Enforcing tests (`tests/symbols.rs`)\n63\t\n64\t| test | what it enforces |\n65\t|------|------------------|\n66\t| `c_and_rust_export_identical_symbol_sets` | the two `nm -D --defined-only` sets are equal, and equal to `{driver, main}` |\n67\t| `c_symbols_are_static_where_the_source_says_static` | neither object exports `print_hex` |\n68\t| `rust_so_has_no_unresolved_non_runtime_symbols` | every undefined symbol in the Rust `.so` is libc/libgcc/TLS runtime (the same classifier is applied to the C `.so`, so it cannot quietly accept everything) |\n69\t| `cargo_built_shared_objects_match_too` | the artifact **cargo** produces (`target/{debug,release}/libdriver.so`) exports the same set; if neither exists it builds one into its own target directory rather than passing vacuously |\n70\t\n71\t`tests/smoke.rs` additionally checks the harness itself: both objects `dlopen`,\n72\tboth symbols resolve and are callable, and every capture mechanism (regular file,\n73\tpipe, forked child, real executables) agrees\n74\t(`both_shared_objects_load_and_export_driver_and_main`,\n75\t`capture_mechanisms_agree`, `forked_main_runner_works`,\n76\t`executables_agree_on_a_simple_input`).\n77\t\n78\tSymbol diff is **empty** — every symbol exported by the C `.so` is exported by\n79\tthe Rust `.so` under the exact same name, and the Rust `.so` exports nothing\n80\textra. Enforced automatically by `tests/symbols.rs`\n81\t(`c_and_rust_export_identical_symbol_sets`), which re-runs `nm -D` on both\n82\tobjects and also checks the cargo-built `target/{debug,release}/libdriver.so`\n83\twhen present.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014BZJRV9mTTLmVbbGcubu9U","session_id":"64daaee6-dfd8-4ebc-87be-dd6361eb86bc","uuid":"f181076b-6647-4182-be56-549e9d1f86aa","timestamp":"2026-08-18T10:36:56.423Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-audit artifacts after fixes"}
