"print_hex\"))`. If `nm` fails, `stdout` is empty and the assertion passes vacuously. `tests/symbols.rs:13-24` does check `out.status.success()` — apply the same there. Minor siblings: `tests/stdin_stream.rs:427` `assert!(f.as_raw_fd() > 2)` asserts nothing about either implementation; `tests/stdin_stream.rs:479-487` silently `return`s if `script(1)` is missing (present here: `util-linux 2.37.4`, so C33b did run).\n\n### 11. [OK-NOTE] Stale/mismatched test prose (no functional impact)\n`tests/main_valid.rs:174-175` still says C18 crosses \"Rust's 8 KiB `BufReader`\" — the design no longer uses a `BufReader`. `tests/driver_valid.rs:147-148` says `c24_driver_state_is_not_sticky` calls `driver` \"before and after a captured batch\"; the body has no batch and never calls `main`, so the \"no state leaks between entry points\" part of C24 rests solely on `c24_main_and_driver_interleaved`. ERRORS.md:56 \"All 18 rows have a passing **differential** test in `tests/error_paths.rs`\" — E14/E15's test is a symbol-absence check, and E18's two tests live in `stdin_stream.rs` (noted parenthetically). ERRORS.md:40 lists `-`+letter as an E4 trigger; that is E6's shape (covered by `e4b_all_byte_values_as_prefix`).\n\n### 12. [OK-NOTE] C27's `[x]` is not earned by `cargo test`\n`cargo test` runs dev-so + dev-cargo only. I ran three of the four legs: dev/dev, `RUST_SO_PROFILE=release` + dev cargo, and dev-so + `--release` cargo — **all 75 pass**. `scripts/verify_all.sh` does implement the full matrix (I read it, did not run it).\n\n---\n\n### Verified correct (item-by-item)\n\n* **Greps (ERRORS.md:9-14, CONFIGS.md:11)** reproduce verbatim: grep 1 → no matches (rc=1); grep 2 → exactly `24:`, `27:`, `41:`; `#if` count → 0; `wc -l` → 41.\n* **All 18 E-rows verified empirically** against my own `gcc 11.5.0 / glibc 2.34` build (requirement was ≥14): E1 `00000000`/0; E2 all six whitespace classes + mixes; E3 `0<&-` and `< .` → `00000000`/0; E4 all 12 listed bytes + the pushback claim (`\"x12