{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_iaz7bbma626kapwibqfshttk4fguzb4524p2hoc7jry23wctvftq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the final state:\n\n## Phase A — surface artifacts (all rows checked off)\n\n| artifact | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | C `.so` exports exactly `driver` + `main`; Rust `.so` exports the same two, nothing more (`print_hex` is `static` in both). Diff empty for `rustc`-built *and* `cargo`-built (debug+release) objects. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 18 rows, mechanically derived (the C file has *one* conditional and *one* `return`, so all rejection lives in `scanf`, the ignored `printf`/`putchar` results, the `long`→`int` narrowing, the absent validation, and the inherited signal disposition). |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 37 rows: `driver` bit-pattern shapes (incl. exhaustive 8⁴, 4×256, 65 536 sweeps), the whole `scanf` input ladder, buffer-boundary sizes, pipe/file/tty/`O_APPEND`/pre-`lseek`/write-only descriptors, repeated & concurrent & re-entrant `main`, locale, profiles. |\n\n## Phase B/C — 80 differential tests in 9 binaries\n\nAll comparisons go through `libloading`-`dlopen`ed exports (or the two real executables) — never a direct Rust call. Fixed **10 real divergences** the C code exposed:\n\n1. **SIGPIPE** — Rust's runtime sets `SIG_IGN`; C dies of signal 13. Now the *inherited* disposition is captured in an ELF constructor and restored (handles `SIG_DFL`, `SIG_IGN` and custom handlers).\n2. **stdin read-ahead was thrown away** (nested `BufReader`), so a second run/reader saw different bytes.\n3. **`ungetc` pushback** lost between conversions (`\"12-34\"` → C's next conversion reads `-34`).\n4. **Exit-time rewind** (`_IO_cleanup`) missing → fd 0 left at a different offset.\n5. **Buffer size** was 8 KiB instead of glibc's `st_blksize` rule (4096 on a pipe, 1024 on a pty).\n6. **`EINTR`** was retried; glibc fails the conversion.\n7. **stdout lock granularity** (one lock per `printf`, not per line).\n8. **Sticky EOF indicator** — after EOF glibc issues no further `read`.\n9. **Conversion atomicity** — a recursive stream lock, so concurrent callers can't split a number and a signal handler can still re-enter.\n10. **Buffer alloc failure** → 1-byte `_shortbuf` fallback instead of aborting.\n\nExternal fuzzing after the fixes: ~80 000 differential cases (parser, locales ×253, fd-shapes, offsets, dlopen sequences, threads) with **0 mismatches**; the only remaining differences are the four explicitly documented ones in CONFIGS.md (\"Deliberately not emulated\": glibc's stdout-flushed-at-exit ordering/loss when a *host* mixes its own stdio or abandons `exit`, a host's own `getchar`/`ungetc`/`feof` on glibc's `stdin`, `atexit`-vs-`dlclose` timing of the rewind, and `vfscanf`'s scratch-buffer OOM under an artificial `RLIMIT_AS`).\n\n## Phase D — parity + all configurations\n\n`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`, so there is exactly one feature combination; `scripts/verify_all.sh` enumerates it (and would enumerate a full powerset if features existed) and runs: 2 `cargo check`s, the CMake + `gcc -shared` C builds, both cargo builds, and the whole suite for `{no-default-features} × {so=dev, so=release} × {cargo=dev, cargo=release}` plus a parallel default run — **ALL 11 STEPS PASSED**, 80/80 tests in every leg. `c_src/` is unmodified (only the prescribed `c_src/build/` output exists)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1123,"cache_read_input_tokens":404385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1123,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64daaee6-dfd8-4ebc-87be-dd6361eb86bc","uuid":"111fe6cc-759c-4954-9940-755a1e7de2c4","timestamp":"2026-08-18T11:36:56.812Z"}
